1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:19,513
They put Tank in a private room with a view of the mountains. I paid
for the room next door for Rosa because she wouldn't leave him. "I'm
here for Shawna," she said. Tank looked at me from his pillows.
"Nigga, tell Shawna I'm doing better." "Shut up." "Tell Shawna you
called me handsome." "You were bleeding.

2
00:00:19,763 --> 00:00:41,775
I was keeping you interested." "Nigga, write that down," Tank told me.
"She's interested." Rosa adjusted his blanket over the bandage, gently
enough that both of us knew better than to mention it. I bought my
nigga a black Cadillac. Then I bought him another because he called
and said the first picture didn't do the color justice.

3
00:00:42,025 --> 00:00:55,267
"Nigga, you buying me a car or showing me a car?" "Look out your
fucking window." Rosa opened the blinds. I heard Tank laugh, stop
because it hurt, then make the bad decision again.

4
00:00:55,517 --> 00:01:18,300
"Two?" "One for whichever side of the hospital you recover on."
"Aiden," Rosa said, "this nigga needs to learn to walk." "That's why I
put them outside." Tank asked her which one she liked. Rosa called him
an idiot and stayed at the window choosing. Nigga, I'd seen that man
take punches that would've put another man's shoes in the obituary.

5
00:01:18,550 --> 00:01:41,441
He'd never sounded as nervous as he did asking whether she preferred
the left Cadillac. I went back to the house with Shawna three days
after Red died. The lake was quiet. There were flowers at the gate,
flowers on the stairs, flowers in the bedroom. Niggas I'd never met
sent bottles and watches. Women sent silk, perfume, diamonds.

6
00:01:41,691 --> 00:02:02,283
Somebody sent a white horse with a blue ribbon tied into its mane. I
had the horse taken around to the back where she could see it from the
balcony. Shawna stood at the bedroom window and looked down at it.
"You buy that?" "Somebody sent it." "Why?" "Because they know who you
are." She watched it walking beside the water.

7
00:02:02,533 --> 00:02:21,922
"I don't know how to ride." "Then we'll learn." She turned toward me.
For a second, I thought she was going to cry again. Then she laughed.
I had missed that sound so bad. I had been hearing gunfire in my
sleep, hearing T say son, hearing Red tell me she'd have got in the
car with anybody.

8
00:02:22,172 --> 00:02:41,047
I had started thinking that was all the world had left to say to me.
Then she laughed and came across the room and kissed me. I picked her
up. She wrapped her arms around my neck, and I carried her away from
the window while the sun went down behind the mountains. My side hurt.
I didn't put her down.

9
00:02:41,297 --> 00:03:03,302
Nigga, I'd carried worse for men who loved me less. Later, we lay
awake listening to the water. Her watch rested on the nightstand. I
looked at it for a while. She saw me looking. "You want me to put it
away?" I didn't answer right away. I wanted everything. Her mornings.
Her nights. The way she turned her head when somebody said my name.

10
00:03:03,552 --> 00:03:21,505
I wanted to be the man she thought of when a song came on. I wanted to
reach back three years and be the one carrying that cake into the
club. I wanted to put myself in every photograph that had ever made
her happy. I couldn't. And all the money in Vegas couldn't help me
with that.

11
00:03:21,755 --> 00:03:41,424
I'd bought half a fucking city, and I couldn't buy one night three
years ago. "No," I said. She rested her head on my chest. "Sometimes I
miss him when I'm happy." I looked at the ceiling. "With me?" "Yeah."
That hurt. I'm not going to lie to you. That shit went straight
through me. She lifted her head.

12
00:03:41,674 --> 00:04:00,341
"Because I wish he knew I wasn't hurting all the time anymore." I
looked at her then. She touched the cross against my chest. "I wish he
knew somebody stayed." I took her hand and held it there. Neither of
us said anything for a long time. Then I asked her to marry me. Right
there.

13
00:04:00,591 --> 00:04:18,119
No shirt, no ring, her dead husband's watch where both of us could see
it. She sat up. "Aiden." "I mean it." "You just bought me a house."
"I'll buy you another one." "That's not what I'm saying." "Then tell
me what you're saying." She looked at me with tears in her eyes.

14
00:04:18,369 --> 00:04:38,725
"You can't fix every bad thing that ever happened to me." "I know."
"You gonna be mad when you find that out for real?" I sat up beside
her. "I'm gonna be mad about a lot of shit, baby. I'm a fucked-up man.
You know that." She nodded. "I'm asking you to marry me, baby. Bring
the watch. Bring the pictures.

15
00:04:38,975 --> 00:04:54,192
Bring every fucking thing you can't leave behind. Just come with me."
She put her hand over my mouth. Then she started laughing and crying
at the same time. "Yes," she said. I kissed her palm. "Say it again."
"Yes.

16
00:04:54,442 --> 00:05:12,169
I'll marry you." I had fifty niggas outside that house ready to die
for me and more money than I could count in one room, and I swear to
you none of it had ever made me feel like that one word. We got
married beside the lake. Three weeks after I walked into the Saint.

17
00:05:12,419 --> 00:05:34,411
The flowers cost more than every rent payment I'd ever made put
together. Shawna came toward me in a white dress while a woman sang
the song she used to sing in her mother's kitchen. Blue roses and the
gardenias I had promised her covered the aisle. There were diamonds at
her throat. Dante's watch on her wrist. I wore the cross.

18
00:05:34,661 --> 00:05:52,580
Tank stood beside me in a black suit with his arm still healing under
the jacket. Rosa sat in the front row wearing a blue dress and trying
not to look at him. He looked at her enough for both of them. Every
table had a bottle of Hennessy on it. Every nigga at the gate had a
gun.

19
00:05:52,830 --> 00:06:09,310
Behind the flowers, my people watched the road while men from other
cities came to shake my hand and find out whether the stories were
true. Nigga, they were true enough that none of them tried me. I paid
the singer more than she asked. Then I paid her band.

20
00:06:09,560 --> 00:06:27,630
Then I bought the place where she'd been playing because Shawna said
the owner had treated her like shit once, years ago, when she was
trying to get an audition. I didn't bring him to the wedding. I made
that nigga listen to it from the parking lot. Shawna reached me and
put her hands in mine.

21
00:06:27,880 --> 00:06:48,446
For a moment I forgot everybody else was there. The preacher asked me
if I would love her in sickness and in health. I looked at the scar
above her eyebrow. At the mark still fading on her mouth. At the wrist
she had held against my bleeding side when all I had to give her was a
promise about a house near the water.

22
00:06:48,696 --> 00:07:07,576
"I will." He asked her the same. "I will." That's how it happened. Her
hand was shaking in mine. Tank kept wiping his face with the sleeve on
his good arm. Rosa was crying into a napkin she'd stolen off his
table. My girl said yes in front of the whole fucking city.

23
00:07:07,826 --> 00:07:26,652
I kissed my wife while the band played and my people shouted my name.
The wedding presents arrived in a convoy longer than the one we'd
taken into the desert. Knox brought a gold-plated pair of handcuffs in
a velvet box and told Shawna she trusted her to decide when they were
necessary.

24
00:07:26,902 --> 00:07:50,977
Shawna held them up, looked at me, and smiled in a way that made Tank
cover his eyes. "Nigga, I'm trying to eat." "Then look at your plate,"
Rosa told him. Professor Halcyon came with Principal Mercer and six
graduates who'd helped carry people out of the auditorium. They
brought a framed photograph of my Lamborghini coming through the doors
with fire behind it.

25
00:07:51,227 --> 00:08:15,232
Mercer had signed the bottom in gold. Our valedictorian. "Nigga, you
signed this like you made me," I told him. He began crying again.
Shawna took the frame before either of us dropped it. "I know exactly
where this goes." "Over the bed?" "Over the fireplace. You already
think enough of yourself in bed." Mercedes screamed laughing. Porsche
nearly dropped her drink.

26
00:08:15,482 --> 00:08:35,140
Mercer didn't seem to understand the sentence, but he nodded like the
academic quality of it was beyond dispute. Rex Crown arrived with a
white limousine full of fighters who all wanted to shake my hand. He
introduced me to each one by telling them exactly how quickly I had
put him down.

27
00:08:35,390 --> 00:08:57,806
Every time he told it, the time got shorter and his expression got
prouder. "One punch," he said to the last man. "Before I got
comfortable." "Rex, nigga, you weren't comfortable when you arrived."
"That's what I'm telling him. I never stood a chance." The fighter
looked at me, looked at Shawna, and bowed his head. "Congratulations,
Captain." "See?" Rex said.

28
00:08:58,056 --> 00:09:22,732
"Nigga learns fast." Little Saint brought a motorcycle painted dark
blue with my initials on the tank. He told me it was for days when
four wheels felt like too much company. Tank immediately told him no
day in my life required fewer wheels. "You jealous?" Little Saint
asked. "Nigga, I have watched this man drive. I am informed." Leon
brought a bicycle.

29
00:09:22,982 --> 00:09:44,311
A real bicycle. Green. A little basket on the front. He wheeled it
through the gate in a tuxedo and looked straight at Porsche. "This one
floats." She kissed him on the cheek. "Baby, so did the first car for
a minute." He shut his eyes while everybody laughed, then opened them
on the house, the music, the lake full of lights.

30
00:09:44,561 --> 00:10:00,847
"I wouldn't have missed any of it," he said. Nigga, neither would I.
For our first dance, Shawna wanted a song she could hear without
remembering a room somebody else had paid for. So we made one. She had
written the melody in the week before the wedding.

31
00:10:01,097 --> 00:10:23,090
I'd found her at the piano after midnight, barefoot, chewing the end
of a pencil while she tried to make the bridge stop sounding like she
was saying goodbye. I sat beside her and played the left hand while
she sang. "There," I said when her voice rose. "Where?" "Don't turn
back. Keep going." She tried it. The note opened. Her face changed.

32
00:10:23,340 --> 00:10:44,088
"Baby." "That's us." We worked until the sun came up. No dead men in
the song. No promises somebody had made with one hand on a door. Just
a woman hearing a car in the driveway and knowing the person she
wanted was finally coming in. Now the band played it beside the lake
while my wife put her hand in mine.

33
00:10:44,338 --> 00:11:05,802
The first steps were easy. The next ones belonged to her. Shawna moved
like music had been waiting all those years for somebody to give her
enough room, and I followed until she laughed at how serious I looked.
"Nigga, you know how to dance." "I know how to dance with you.
Different subject. Higher degree." She leaned back in my arm.

34
00:11:06,051 --> 00:11:27,065
I caught her, turned, brought her close again while the whole wedding
cheered. Rosa stood up first. Tank tried to follow and remembered his
shoulder. She came to him instead, took his good hand, and led him
onto the edge of the floor. "I don't dance," he told her. "You do
tonight." "Rosa—" "Nigga, you got shot for these people.

35
00:11:27,315 --> 00:11:50,523
Survive four steps with me." He survived them. Badly at first. Then
better when he stopped looking at his feet and looked at her face. I
watched my brother discover that being large wasn't the only way to
take up a woman's whole world. He looked over at me once, embarrassed
and helplessly happy. I nodded. Your nigga got it, I was telling him.

36
00:11:50,773 --> 00:12:12,195
Your nigga had finally fucking got it. At the last chorus, the
fireworks began over the water. Blue and gold. Huge flowers opening in
the sky above the house I'd bought before I knew where to put my own
clothes. The guests turned to look. Shawna stayed looking at me. I put
my forehead against hers.

37
00:12:12,445 --> 00:12:32,798
"You missing the expensive part." "No, baby." She touched the cross.
"I'm looking right at him." Nigga, I didn't have a single smart thing
left in my mouth. She kissed me before I could find one. Then we went
inside and got so drunk the sun came up before anybody remembered
there had been a schedule.

38
00:12:33,048 --> 00:12:56,453
There was cocaine in the upstairs bathroom, cash changing hands on the
terrace, hookers dancing with men who had brought other women to the
wedding. Somebody drove a convertible onto the lawn. Tank fell asleep
with his good arm around Rosa, and she threatened to kill the first
motherfucker who took a picture. I bought every picture the next
morning. I kept one.

39
00:12:56,703 --> 00:13:15,219
Nigga looks at it now and swears he was awake. Rosa has the same
picture by her bed. People tell this story like everything ended when
Red hit the ground. It didn't. The calls kept coming. The money kept
coming. The west side still needed a boss on Monday.

40
00:13:15,469 --> 00:13:30,609
A man in another city still thought Red dying meant he could take what
Red used to sell. Somebody still owed somebody, and somebody's brother
still wanted blood. I didn't become a good man because I put a ring on
Shawna's finger.

41
00:13:30,859 --> 00:13:48,511
I was still the nigga who walked into a hotel with blood on his collar
and told another man's people the girl was coming with him. I still
had a temper. Still had a gun. Still woke up some nights with my hand
on the place T had shot me. And I still wanted everything.

42
00:13:48,761 --> 00:14:10,626
But now I knew who I was bringing it home to. One night that week, I
came back from handling business and found Shawna in the room we'd
made for her music. She had all the lights off except the little lamp
beside the piano. There were papers on the floor. A half-finished
drink on the windowsill. She was singing something I hadn't heard
before.

43
00:14:10,876 --> 00:14:31,255
I stood in the doorway and listened. When she finished, she turned
around. "How long you been there?" "Long enough." "You like it?"
"Yeah." "You always say that." "I always mean it." She held out her
hand. I went to her. Outside, there were niggas guarding the gates and
a city waiting for me to make the next decision.

44
00:14:31,505 --> 00:14:48,494
In that room, she pulled me down beside her and put my hand against
her heart. "Stay a minute," she said. I stayed all night. Aight, my
nigga. Now you know which nigga you riding with. You know about the
money in the pool. You know about the blood in the car.

45
00:14:48,744 --> 00:15:07,272
You know why I wear a dead man's cross and why my wife still wears his
watch. You know which nigga called me son and tried to kill me, and
which nigga took a bullet before he'd let me stand alone. Don't let
anybody tell you I came out of that desert clean. I came out alive.

46
00:15:07,522 --> 00:15:27,859
I came out with Shawna's hand in mine and Tank bleeding in the back of
an ambulance, and I made the whole fucking city learn our names. My
nigga, I gave away the most expensive diamond I ever held. Then I took
everything the man wearing it thought he was going to leave behind.
That's what happened.

47
00:15:28,109 --> 00:15:44,424
That's my money in the walls of that house. That's my name on the
cars. That's my wife singing with the window open when the lake goes
black at night. And when she wakes up crying, I'm there. When Tank
calls me at three in the morning, I answer.

48
00:15:44,674 --> 00:16:03,691
When some motherfucker thinks the years made me soft, I let him get
close enough to see the scar. You can call that love. You can call
that crazy. Call it whatever the fuck you want. I was crazy before she
loved me. I had blood on me before she touched me. She didn't make me
dangerous.

49
00:16:03,941 --> 00:16:25,719
She gave all that danger somewhere to come home. I remember Dante. I
never met him, but I remember him every time that gold cross hits my
chest. I remember T. I wish I could remember him without the gun. I
remember Red. I remember what he looked like when he found out there
was something in that room he couldn't buy.

50
00:16:25,969 --> 00:16:47,505
And I remember her in the Mercedes. One hand on the wheel. One hand
trying to keep my life inside me. She could've left me. She could've
taken what she could carry and gone. But she stayed. My girl stayed.
So your nigga stayed too. What the fuck else was I going to do with a
home? Ten toes down, my nigga.

51
00:16:47,755 --> 00:17:06,558
In the club where twelve niggas tried me. In the desert where thirty
engines answered. In that hospital hallway waiting for my nigga Tank
to open his eyes and start requesting Cadillacs. A nigga can stand in
a kingdom; a nigga can stand beside a bed. I stood in both.

52
00:17:06,809 --> 00:17:27,024
Ten toes down when the money came, and ten toes down when no nigga
could buy the thing I was waiting to hear. And if another man comes
through that gate thinking he's going to make her cry like that again,
he better bring every goddamn prayer he knows. Because I'm home now.
Aiden. Ten toes down. Forever.

53
00:17:27,274 --> 00:17:50,889
The invitation arrived the morning we were packing for our honeymoon.
Blue envelope. Silver seal. Nobody had come through the gate. It lay
on the hood of my police Lamborghini when I came outside carrying
Shawna's suitcase and my smaller bag. Tank pointed at it. "If that's
another college, I'm taking the test." "Nigga, start with the
envelope." He picked it up.

54
00:17:51,139 --> 00:18:16,724
"Sky High." "Club?" "School." "Nigga, I just graduated. They got a
return policy?" Shawna came down with Rosa on her arm. Mercedes and
Porsche stood by the cars arguing over suitcases. Mercedes had brought
enough to make a nigga check whether somebody had sold her apartment.
"It's their honeymoon," Porsche said. "I'm aware." "Then why you have
four bags?" "Because I'm aware it's their honeymoon.

55
00:18:16,974 --> 00:18:41,904
I need my own activities." Marcellus stood beside the white horse,
feeding it something the trainer had approved. Blue Mercy was safe in
a proper case, and the old nigga had finally stopped carrying the case
from room to room. He let the horse finish chewing before he looked
over. "Trouble?" "Education," Tank said. "Ah. Expensive trouble." I
opened the envelope. A photograph slid out.

56
00:18:42,154 --> 00:19:07,977
Campus. Lawns. Football field. Towers. All above the clouds, on a huge
piece of ground with no apparent interest in rejoining the rest of the
fucking planet. Tank bent over it. "Nigga, that's up." "I see." "No.
That's UP up. Our school had steps. These niggas got weather." Rosa
took the photograph. "What's underneath it?" "A lawsuit if a nigga
drops his keys," Mercedes said.

57
00:19:08,227 --> 00:19:32,679
The letter came from Dean Seraphine Storm. Advanced adult hero
program. Every incoming student at least twenty-two. She'd seen the
graduation footage, the hospital rescue, the convoy, and enough of my
other work to think I'd been taking the long way to the right school.
She wanted me after the honeymoon. She wanted my people too. I read
that again. My people.

58
00:19:32,929 --> 00:19:57,448
Nigga, I liked a dean who understood the application included
attachments. "All of us?" Tank asked. I handed him the page. He read
it, then looked at Rosa, trying to make the looking casual. Rosa
pointed at the photograph. "They got rooms?" "Whole residences,"
Shawna said, reading the next page. "Piano?" I asked. "Conservatory."
"That's more piano?" "Yes, baby.

59
00:19:57,698 --> 00:20:20,411
More piano." Porsche took off her sunglasses. "Cars?" I found the
line. Your automobile may accompany you, Captain. We would prefer that
its first landing be supervised. "Nigga," Tank said, "they know you
personally." I started smiling. Shawna caught it. "Honeymoon first."
"Absolutely." "A real honeymoon. With a bed. The bed touches a floor.

60
00:20:20,661 --> 00:20:44,646
The floor touches the fucking earth." "Whatever my wife wants." "And
when I say beach, I mean beach. You will not enroll the sand in
college." "Baby, if the sand tests well—" She held out her hand for
the keys. I gave them to her. Nigga, marriage was going beautifully.
Clear expectations. Prompt consequences. Tank handed back the
photograph.

61
00:20:44,896 --> 00:21:09,476
"You think you can be best in that school too?" I folded the letter
beside my badge. The gold cross settled against my chest. "Tank."
"What?" "Those niggas invited me. They know." Shawna opened the
Lamborghini. "Get in, valedictorian. I'm driving before somebody gives
you a planet." I got in. My niggas were still arguing over luggage. My
wife was starting the engine.

62
00:21:09,726 --> 00:21:23,131
A college in the sky wanted the whole unreasonable collection of us.
Nigga, I had a wife, a badge, a kingdom, and somewhere new to be
magnificent. And she still made me carry the bags.
